&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;Hello there,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;i couldnt find a nice backpack fitting my custom miniatures for star wars legion iam designing so i decided to make my own. I tried to model it after what the official rebel troopers had on, so i guess this would fit any setting, scifi or fantasy. I haven&amp;#39;t test printed it yet so i&amp;#39;ll be adding pictures of the printed backpack later. (with Anycubic Photon)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;I added the stl as well the obj file so feel free to customize for your own personal purpose.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;Like and comment if you like it :)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;PS: i used the same suffix &amp;#34;Sculptris OBJ Bits&amp;#34; as dutchmogul so anybody who might want to add this to his mini in sculptris might find it. If you&amp;#39;re looking for custom mini parts definetely check his collection. I&amp;#39;am using his body parts for upcoming model remixes.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
